   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the retirement and social security law and the workers'\ncompensation law, in relation to extending the deadline for submission of a\nnotice that a member of a retirement system participated in World Trade Center\nrescue, recovery or cleanup operations",
    "basePrintNo": "S10605",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10605-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, R & SS L; amd §§162 & 168, Work Comp L",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10605\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law and the workers'\ncompensation law, in relation to extending the deadline for submission\nof a notice that a member of a retirement system participated in World\nTrade Center rescue, recovery or cleanup operations\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends paragraph (a) of subdivision 36 of section 2 of the\nretirement and social security law to update the definition of \"qualify-\ning World Trade Center condition\" to allow a member of a retirement\nsystem who participated in World Trade Center rescue, recovery or clean-\nup operations, or their eligible beneficiary in the case of the member's\ndeath, to file a statement indicating the underlying dates and locations\nof employment no later than September 11, 2030.\n\nSection 2 amends section 162 of the workers' compensation law to allow a\nparticipant in World Trade Center rescue, recovery and clean-up oper-\nations to file a written and sworn statement with the Workers' Compen-\nsation Board indicating the dates and locations of such participation\nand the name of such participant's employer during the period of partic-\nipation by September 11, 2030.\n\nSection 3 amends section 168 of the workers' compensation law by adding\na new subdivision 6, which states that a claim by a participant in World\nTrade Center rescue, recovery or cleanup operations whose disablement\noccurred between September 11, 2021 and September 11, 2025, shall not be\ndisallowed as barred by section 18 or section 28 of the workers' compen-\nsation law if such claim is filed on or before September 11, 2030.\nClaims for disablement during this period that were disallowed by\nsection 18 or section 28 shall be reconsidered.\n\nSection 4 states that notwithstanding any other provision to the contra-\nry, none of the provisions of this act shall be subject to section 25 of\nthe retirement and social security law.\n\nSection 5 provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill extends the deadline to submit a World Trade Center Notice to\nthe relevant retirement system to 2030. It would also allow any partic-\nipant in World Trade Center rescue, recovery or cleanup operations who\nwas disabled between September 11, 2021 and September 11, 2025 to file a\nclaim by September 11, 2030. If a participant filed a claim in this\nperiod and it was disallowed, the Workers' Compensation Board shall\nreconsider it.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2022: Chapter 561\n\n2018: Chapter 266\n\n2015: S.5745 - Passed Senate\n2013: Chapter 489\n\n2008: Chapter 489\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee fiscal notes.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall be deemed to have been\nin full force and effect on and after September 11, 2001; provided,\nhowever, that the amendments to sections 162 and 168 of the workers'\ncompensation law made by sections two and three of this act, respective-\nly, shall apply to all open and closed claims coming within the purview\nof the workers' compensation board.\n",
